Original image 216px-salsa-clip-art-916484.gif downloaded
from cliparthut.com with the usage statement:
"Free cliparts all used for FREE"

I edited the colors using the Gimp, using burnt orange and white,
the burnt orange color as specified by the UT web site, which is
#BF5700.

I created the SALSA text using the site http://cooltext.com/  This was
using their "fun" font and again inserting the UT burnt orange color,
tweaking a few things along the way.  Usage terms:
You are welcome to use any of the generated graphics in any way, 
shape, or form without asking permission.

The gimp file (salsa.xcf) has two layers with transparency.  To produce
the windows icon file (salsa_icon.ico), I merged visible layers, then
used the export function to produce the ico file, deselecting compression.
Then exit gimp without saving so as to preserve the 2-layer configuration
in the source.

To my understanding, any win7 or later computer should handle the 256x256
file just fine and will down-scale when appropriate.
